        },
        "name": "Output ratio"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_KF9RDZDA5A4G44VS082816ZH4A",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 1 \u2014 subject is cut out, destination plates come in separately, and the relight director reconciles them."
        },
        "name": "Stage 1"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_MHR01JBC7VGV8TXTZ6RNBWKZP4",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 2100,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 2 \u2014 composite renders, then upscales before download."
        },
        "name": "Stage 2"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_DMH88WKF4W315B3M7EC8T5FSWW",
        "kind": "bg-remove",
        "position": {
          "x": 700,
          "y": 300
        },
        "config": {},
        "name": "Cut out subject"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_8QSQ3EPXNPA11V8D1KYQQ3ZB71",
        "kind": "download",
        "position": {
          "x": 2800,
          "y": 420
        },
        "config": {
          "appendable_slots": {
            "images": 2
          }
        },
        "name": "Composites"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_TH1W5H6MCTB0T0PEPFM3GG1BJM",
        "kind": "text-gen",
        "position": {
          "x": 1400,
          "y": 180
        },
        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 1300,
          "temperature": 0.48,
          "system_prompt": "You are the compositing and relighting director placing an armchair into a new environment.\n\nINPUTS. Reference slot one is the cut-out subject with its background already removed; the remaining slots are the destination plate: workshop pegboard (high-key key).\n\nMATCH. Your prompt must force the subject's light to match the plate: state the key direction in degrees, the colour temperature difference, the shadow softness and length, and where the contact shadow grounds the object. A composite fails on contact shadow and edge light before anything else.\n\nCAMERA MATCH. Reconcile perspective and lens: 20mm wide at f/4, matching horizon height and the plate's depth of field falloff.\n\nINTEGRATION. Call for matching grain, matching chromatic aberration at the edges, spill light from the plate onto the subject, and a filmic grade with halation on the specular highlights.\n\nPRESERVE. Do not alter the subject's shape, colourway or printed label in any way.\n\nOUTPUT. Emit one prompt, one paragraph, no framing text of any kind before or after it.\n\nVARIANT. This branch renders a high-key treatment with an almost shadowless base and clean separation.",
          "appendable_slots": {
            "reference_images": 2
          }
        },
        "name": "Relight director 1"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_YE9PHXHASWPH3GWRMSM30HMCQZ",
        "kind": "image-gen",
        "position": {
